course: dictionary
lesson: 7211
title: Philippine: from the Philippines
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Philippine is an adjective, so it describes a thing that belongs to, or comes from, the Philippines. «Only a few hundred pairs of Philippine eagles are thought to live in the forests of the Philippines.» The word Philippine tells you which eagles we mean: the eagles of that country.
explain: Look at the two forms. Philippine, with no s, describes things: the Philippine Islands, the Philippine flag. The Philippines, with an s and a capital P, is the name of the country itself. A quick check: if you can say "of the Philippines" after the word, it is the adjective Philippine.
explain: Context gives you more clues. The sentence says the eagles are rare because of forest cutting and hunting, and that they are protected by law. So a Philippine eagle is a special bird that needs care. Swap in your meaning: "the eagle from the Philippines" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: The Philippines is a country in Southeast Asia.
fact: The Philippines is made of more than 7,000 islands.
fact: Philippine means belonging to or coming from the Philippines.
fact: The people of the Philippines are called Filipinos.
fact: The Philippine eagle is the national bird, and it is protected by law.
exercise: Which word describes a thing from the Philippines, like «the Philippine flag»? | *Philippine | Filipinos | Pacific | Philippines
exercise: Which word is the name of the country itself? | Philippine | Filipino | Philippine Sea | *The Philippines
exercise: Which phrase names something Philippine? | A desert camel | Pancakes from Paris | *The Philippine Sea | A Scottish castle
test: What is the Philippines? | A river in Africa | A type of tree | *A country in Southeast Asia made of more than 7,000 islands | A city in Italy
test: Why is the Philippine eagle protected by law? | It is the smallest bird in the world | It can talk like a parrot | *Forest cutting and hunting have made it rare | It lives only in busy cities
exam: Which word fits? «The ___ eagle is the national bird.» | Japanese | *Philippine | Scottish | Italian
